From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: playportdev <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 18:32:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: route SocialClubHelper.exe's large reservations into
 the Social Club layout

PLA-476, active only with PLAYPORT_SC_LAYOUT=1 and a complete boot layout.
The helper is recognised by its image name only, not by 0150's exact-build
check: that verdict is a thread-local of the child's first thread, cleared
once its image is mapped, so no allocating thread can read it, and carrying
it per process is a change of its own. SocialClubHelper.exe's
chrome_elf/libcef PartitionAlloc pools, their metadata regions, Oilpan's
cage and V8's 8 GB sandbox step get fixed real slots and report what was
asked; Oilpan's slot and the V8 cage go only to the helper that holds both
core pools. Every other giant reserve from the helper fails with
STATUS_NO_MEMORY instead of reaching the soft-pool grant (PLA-477).

A grant gives back its native hold and places a Wine view in the slot with
no-replace semantics: the slots lie in no Wine reserved area (checked), so
map_fixed_area maps with VM_FLAGS_FIXED, and a native mapping that took the
slot in between makes the grant fail with STATUS_NO_MEMORY, untouched.

Commits, protects and frees inside a slot's real range are allowed only for
its owner; a grant is released as a whole by its owner or at its owner's
exit through the existing process teardown, and the slot is held again.
Operations in reported extents outside the real ranges are logged, not
refused (PLA-482): a commit in a reported tail, one in the lower half of
Oilpan's report (chrome_elf's), one that lands in another slot the same
helper owns, and one on another owner's view, each limited per kind. At an
owner's exit a kept slot view is logged with its owner and committed
extent. The helper is told a 2 TB HighestUserAddress so V8 takes its
partial sandbox (report only). One helper owns the slots at a time.

Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-29-sc-stock-cef-probe.md
Offered-upstream: no
